  "note_m_knowledge": "the multiplier strategy needs m, the attacker's own episode arity. On LSPR23 every host pair carrying attack traffic is 100% malicious, so m is exactly the attacker's own flow count; on a benign-inclusive stream m also contains benign flows and the attacker knows only a lower bound",
  "scope": "multiplier arm covers the windows for which t48_W3 stores per-episode arities (0.55, 0.85, both orders); the absolute arm covers the canonical and first-flow cells of every window and seed t28b carries, not its `keyed` arm. The replication window 0.62 has no stored per-episode m, so it appears in the absolute arm only",
  "note_multiplier_selection": "the per-window minimum c is chosen AFTER seeing the realised overshoot factors and is an oracle-informed floor; the pre-committed claim is the single constant c that defeats every canonical alert at both windows, which is c=10"
 }
}